        },
        "chunks": [
          {
            "chunk_type": "isnad",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "A number of our companions, from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Khalid, from Isma'il ibn Mihran, from Yunus ibn Ya'qub, from Abu Maryam al-Ansari, from Abu Ja'far (AS), who said:",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 27,
            "word_start": 0
          },
          {
            "chunk_type": "opening",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "A man from al-Basra stood up before Amir al-Momineen (AS) and said: 'O Amir al-Momineen (AS)! Inform us about the brethren.' So he (AS) said: 'The brethren are of two types – the trustworthy brethren and the friendly brethren.'",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 49,
            "word_start": 27
          },
          {
            "chunk_type": "body",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "As for the trustworthy brethren, they are the palm, the wing, the family, and the wealth. So when you are with a brother of yours who is at the limit of trustworthiness, then spend your wealth and your body for him, be sincere to those who are sincere to him, and be an adversary to those who are his adversaries, and conceal his secrets and his faults, and manifest the good that is in him. And know, O questioner, that they are scarcer than red sulfur.",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 88,
            "word_start": 49
          },
          {
            "chunk_type": "body",
            "translations": {
              "bn": "",
              "de": "",
              "en": "And as for the friendly brethren, you attain your pleasure from them, so do not sever that from them, nor seek what lies beyond that from their consciences; and exert for them what they exert for you of a cheerful countenance and a sweet tongue.'",
              "es": "",
              "fa": "",
              "fr": "",
              "id": "",
              "ru": "",
              "tr": "",
              "ur": "",
              "zh": ""
            },
            "word_end": 116,
            "word_start": 88
          }
        ],
