        "key_terms": {
          "bn": {},
          "de": {},
          "en": {
            "إِخْوَانُ الثِّقَةِ": "Trustworthy brethren – those with whom the bond of true trust has been established, obligating full commitment of wealth, body, loyalty, and the guarding of their secrets and faults",
            "إِخْوَانُ الْمُكَاشَرَةِ": "Friendly brethren – those with whom one maintains pleasant outward social interaction, without entailing the deeper obligations of sincere brotherhood",
            "الثِّقَةُ": "Trustworthiness/trust – the defining quality that elevates a social relationship to the highest rank of brotherhood, warranting total devotion",
            "الضَّمِيرُ": "Conscience/inner self – the private inner convictions and hidden intentions that one must not probe or demand access to in the case of friendly brethren",
            "الْجَنَاحُ": "The wing – a metaphor for the sheltering, elevating, and encompassing care that the trustworthy brother provides",
            "الْكَفُّ": "The palm – a metaphor for the practical protection, support, and outstretched help that the trustworthy brother provides",
            "الْكِبْرِيتُ الْأَحْمَرُ": "Red sulfur (al-kibrit al-ahmar) – a classical Arabic proverb denoting something of extreme and legendary rarity, here applied to the scarcity of truly trustworthy brethren",
            "طَلَاقَةُ الْوَجْهِ": "Cheerfulness of the countenance – the open, pleasant facial expression that constitutes the appropriate currency of exchange in friendly social relations"
          },
