        "seo_questions": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "What did Imam Ali (AS) say about the two types of brothers and friends in Islam?",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
        "summaries": {
          "bn": "",
          "de": "",
          "en": "Imam 'Ali (AS), responding to a question posed in al-Basra as reported by Imam Abu Ja'far (AS), divides human brethren into two categories: the trustworthy brethren (ikhwan al-thiqa), who are as rare as red sulfur and toward whom one must devote wealth, body, loyalty, and the guarding of secrets; and the friendly brethren (ikhwan al-mukashara), with whom one maintains cordial social pleasantries without expecting or demanding deeper commitment. This hadith establishes a refined ethical framework for navigating human relationships, distinguishing sincere brotherhood from mere social affability.",
          "es": "",
          "fa": "",
          "fr": "",
          "id": "",
          "ru": "",
          "tr": "",
          "ur": "",
          "zh": ""
        },
